meta {
  name: Disconnect
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

delete {
  url: {{baseURL}}/google-calendar/disconnect/
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
}

docs {
  Revokes the token with Google and clears the signed-in associate's own
  google_access_token / google_refresh_token / google_access_token_expires_at.
  Associate.google_email (the "connected as ___" address) is deliberately left
  as a record of the last-connected account — check google_refresh_token, not
  google_email, to know if an associate is actually connected. Always acts on
  request.user.associate - never a client-supplied id.

  If the signed-in associate is the fixed shared calendar organizer
  (Associate.google_email == settings.GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID), disconnecting kills
  appointment sync for every center — so this is only allowed when that
  associate also holds is_admin=True on at least one center assignment.
  Otherwise: 403.

  Method: DELETE
  Path: /google-calendar/disconnect/
  Source: integrations.google_calendar.views.GoogleCalendarDisconnectView
  Auth: Associate (JWT).
}
